"""tinycap interface contracts — the names every lane codes against.

Nothing here does I/O, scoring or dispatch — that lives in the lane
modules named in :data:`DISPATCH_MODULE_OF_CONTROL` — but this module is NOT
constants-only any more: beside the names and schemas it carries EXECUTABLE
contract behaviour that every lane must agree on byte for byte — the
per-task thinking policy
(``thinking_of_task`` / ``battery_thinking`` / ``check_thinking_arg``),
identity construction (``sampling_identity``, ``container_name``,
``cell_out_dir``, the hashed-field tuples), parsing (``parse_launcher_cell``,
``expand_control``, ``parse_replace_source``, ``reduction_mode_from_env``) and
the quality / attestation contracts (``check_reduction_mode_expectation``,
``sampling_for``). Pure functions of their arguments, tested in
``tests/test_tinycap_contracts.py``; a behaviour two lanes would otherwise
each implement belongs here, a behaviour one lane owns does not.

Lane ownership:

* **A** — ``serving/prefill_logprob.py`` (bodies),
  ``scripts/served_capability_run.py`` dispatch + flags, their tests and
  ``tests/fixtures/capeval/served/*``.
* **B** — ``tiers/inspect_served.py`` (the ``tinycap`` Inspect provider,
  preflight, seeded solver, results adapter), ``configs/capeval/
  inspect_tasks/*``, the ``vllm_server`` reasoning-parser knob and the
  ``capctrl_serving_up`` ``--reasoning-parser`` passthrough.
* **C** — ``serving/proxy_engine.py``, ``tiers/evalplus_runner.py``
  (MBPP+, dataset switch), ``scripts/modal/tinycap_sandbox.py``,
  ``scripts/compare_served_hf_task.py``, ``tiers/pairing.py``.
* **D** — ``serving/geometry.py`` (sole owner of the sub-entries and the
  ``n_rejected`` basis field), ``serving/usage_ledger.py``,
  ``scripts/modal/tinycap_served.py``, ``scripts/tinycap_geometry_measure.py``,
  the compiled client lock + its test, ``domains.yaml`` / tier tests,
  ``docs/served_geometry_p99.md`` §6.

Rules that shape every name below:

* Steered numbers come ONLY through the served declared-response-prefill
  path (E6): every prefill-scored request on a lens route carries
  :data:`RESPONSE_PREFILL_KEY`; ``n=`` is never sent (E4); the five
  :data:`FORBIDDEN_CLIENT_KEYS` are never sent (E3); ``stream`` is never
  true.
* ``ROW_COLUMNS`` is frozen — every new per-row fact rides in
  ``extra_json``; the cell ``manifest.json`` is free-form beyond
  ``CellStore.RESUME_KEYS``, so the new blocks are additive keys.
* Completion identity is ``(task, item_id, metric)``
  (``CellStore.completed_keys``), which is why avg@k per-sample rows carry
  the sample index IN THE METRIC NAME (:func:`sample_metric`) and the
  per-item mean keeps the bare metric.
* Virtual-model names are READ from the routing table and preflighted
  against ``/v1/models``, never typed (P20): this module names the CELL
  ids (:data:`ROUTE_NONE_CELL`), not the ``petri__…`` strings.
* No launcher literal window: geometry comes from
  ``sisteer.capeval.serving.geometry``; this module only names the
  sub-entry KEYS Lane D registers.
"""

